"The map generator (server/src/asset/location_map.rs, generate_entities) assumes production-shaped location map themes and panics / hangs the module when given a minimal test theme. Reproduced in E2E: a mapPack with mainRoomCount 3, loopCount 0, a theme with single-blob room/path selectors and small decoration counts caused the module to become unresponsive (client connect timed out), so E2E phases 2-3 had to be switched to direct-seeded worlds instead of exercising the generator. Likely culprits to investigate: decoration-count sampling when maxDecorationCount is small/zero (nextInt(min, max-1) with an empty/inverted range) and sampling from an empty/tiny weighted selector (weighted_sampler / rng_range edge cases). Make generate_entities robust to minimal themes (0 or few rooms/paths/decorations, single-selection or empty selectors) without panicking. Then add an E2E map-generation phase (web-trpg/e2e) that seeds a tiny deterministic map via a test-specific AssetPack (fixed rngSeed) and asserts the expected room/path graph -- restoring generator coverage on test assets, not production content. Capture module panics via spacetime logs while reproducing."